    {
      "id": "25db93a0-35cd-43b3-8205-bf6cabe767fa",
      "name": "Sticky Note Main Description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -512,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 764,
        "height": 884,
        "content": "# Send HeyReach campaign performance reports to Gmail\n\n### Who's it for\nThis template is for sales automation teams, outreach managers, and lead-generation agencies using HeyReach for LinkedIn campaigns.\n\n### How it works / What it does\nWhen HeyReach sends a campaign-completed webhook, the workflow extracts the campaign ID, retrieves campaign statistics, formats a readable HTML performance report, and sends it to Gmail. The report includes connection acceptance, message replies, interested leads, and a campaign link.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Connect your **HeyReach API credential** and **Gmail account** in n8n.\n2. Open **Set Campaign & Recipient Info** and replace `your-email@example.com` with the address that should receive reports.\n3. Copy the production URL from **When HeyReach Campaign Completes**.\n4. In HeyReach, create a **Campaign Completed** webhook under **Integrations → Public API / Webhooks** and paste the URL.\n5. Activate the workflow and complete a test campaign or send a test webhook.\n\n### Requirements\n- An active HeyReach account with webhook access\n- A Gmail account connected in n8n\n\n### How to customize\n- Change the recipient email in **Set Campaign & Recipient Info**.\n- Edit the report text and metrics in **Prepare HTML Email Report**.\n- Replace Gmail with another email provider if needed.\n\n### Security\nCredentials stay in n8n credentials and are not embedded in the HTTP Request node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "772b37a9-082f-4819-8e62-cdb2e45d5240",
      "name": "Step 1 — Connect HeyReach and Gmail",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -512,
        608
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Step 1 — Connect accounts\n\nOpen the credential fields in **Fetch Campaign Stats from HeyReach** and **Send Report via Gmail**. Select or create your HeyReach API and Gmail credentials. Never paste API keys directly into node parameters."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9e2bb4b7-a32c-4505-988c-8fa7c270b7b0",
      "name": "Step 2 — Configure recipient",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -64,
        608
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Step 2 — Choose the recipient\n\nIn **Set Campaign & Recipient Info**, replace `your-email@example.com` with the inbox that should receive completed-campaign reports. This is the only workflow field most users need to change."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3c909ace-bbe5-4279-9338-7829123f6bb8",
      "name": "Step 3 — Add HeyReach webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        384,
        608
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 260,
        "content": "## Step 3 — Connect the webhook\n\nCopy the production URL from **When HeyReach Campaign Completes**. In HeyReach, add a **Campaign Completed** webhook under **Integrations → Public API / Webhooks**. Activate this workflow before sending live events."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
